he subjects they describe, so &ldquo;Rabinal Ach&iacute;&rdquo; needs to be the first word after the comma.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect. This doesn&rsquo;t complete the text in a way that conforms to the conventions of Standard English. The modifier &ldquo;Based on events&hellip;by a king,&rdquo; is describing the drama &ldquo;Rabinal Ach&iacute;.&rdquo; Modifiers need to be next to the subjects they describe, so &ldquo;Rabinal Ach&iacute;&rdquo; needs to be the first word after the comma.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-631-SEC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"4b241b0a-d74f-404b-abf1-8af69aa5ac2b","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959340,"updateDate":1691007959340}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959340, 1691007959340),
    ($SATQ$f0f9bf8f$SATQ$, $SATQ$e2571e58-9647-4c76-bee1-1ffb191506d2$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres debuted his sculpture <em>&ldquo;Untitled&rdquo; (USA Today)</em> in New York City in 1990. The work consists of piled candy, a material Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres became known for. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> created additional installations using a variety of sweets, like bubblegum, lollipops, and chocolates.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ea4f482b-3747-436b-9bbd-d91c0b47c487","content":"<p>They all</p>"},{"id":"d505e0be-63c3-4e76-8882-65495222a8c8","content":"<p>Those</p>"},{"id":"c386d9e0-49d1-4831-b23b-2c6f88e50f90","content":"<p>Both</p>"},{"id":"8f114605-9ed3-4125-bdde-eaa0157aae2e","content":"<p>He</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8f114605-9ed3-4125-bdde-eaa0157aae2e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The convention being tested is pronoun-antecedent agreement. The singular pronoun "he" agrees in number with the singular antecedent "F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres," and it clearly indicates that Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres created the additional installations.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the plural noun phrase "they all" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular antecedent "F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres," and it doesn&rsquo;t clearly indicate that he (Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres) created the additional installations. Choice B is incorrect because the plural pronoun "those" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular antecedent "F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres," and it doesn&rsquo;t clearly indicate that he (Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres) created the additional installations. Choice C is incorrect because the plural pronoun "both" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular antecedent "F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres," and it doesn&rsquo;t clearly indicate that he (Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres) created the additional installations.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f0f9bf8f","external_id":"e2571e58-9647-4c76-bee1-1ffb191506d2","vaultid":null,"uId":"706b652a-ca8c-4c31-8519-14bac62e0e3d","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"FSS","skill_desc":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres debuted his sculpture <em>&ldquo;Untitled&rdquo; (USA Today)</em> in New York City in 1990. The work consists of piled candy, a material Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres became known for. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> created additional installations using a variety of sweets, like bubblegum, lollipops, and chocolates.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ea4f482b-3747-436b-9bbd-d91c0b47c487","content":"<p>They all</p>"},{"id":"d505e0be-63c3-4e76-8882-65495222a8c8","content":"<p>Those</p>"},{"id":"c386d9e0-49d1-4831-b23b-2c6f88e50f90","content":"<p>Both</p>"},{"id":"8f114605-9ed3-4125-bdde-eaa0157aae2e","content":"<p>He</p>"}],"keys":["8f114605-9ed3-4125-bdde-eaa0157aae2e"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The convention being tested is pronoun-antecedent agreement. The singular pronoun \"he\" agrees in number with the singular antecedent \"F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres,\" and it clearly indicates that Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres created the additional installations.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the plural noun phrase \"they all\" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular antecedent \"F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres,\" and it doesn&rsquo;t clearly indicate that he (Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres) created the additional installations. Choice B is incorrect because the plural pronoun \"those\" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular antecedent \"F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres,\" and it doesn&rsquo;t clearly indicate that he (Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres) created the additional installations. Choice C is incorrect because the plural pronoun \"both\" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular antecedent \"F&eacute;lix Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres,\" and it doesn&rsquo;t clearly indicate that he (Gonz&aacute;lez-Torres) created the additional installations.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323050,"updateDate":1730147323050}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323050, 1730147323050),
    ($SATQ$f10b7ce4$SATQ$, $SATQ$5b4f4d25-c4a2-4d33-b71e-ad72e9443a44$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In the list &ldquo;Adorable Things&rdquo; from Sei Shōnagon&rsquo;s&nbsp;<em>Pillow Book</em>, the author delights in baby sparrows, a face drawn on a melon, and a young courtier in ceremonial garb. So shrewd an observer is Shōnagon, a lady-in-waiting to Empress Teishi, that her book&rsquo;s musings on tenth-century Japanese courtly life <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> readers a thousand years later.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"58a90707-9903-49bc-bebc-aed829e1236b","content":"<p>fascinate</p>"},{"id":"938d86f4-c451-4fe0-b023-34e9be3ead87","content":"<p>has fascinated</p>"},{"id":"2e43700e-d679-44e9-8d1d-c4b475b33335","content":"<p>fascinates</p>"},{"id":"469cb5b7-8539-4f9d-b58a-371931f343b1","content":"<p>is fascinating</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["58a90707-9903-49bc-bebc-aed829e1236b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is subject-verb agreement. The plural verb "fascinate" agrees in number with the plural subject "musings."</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the singular verb "has fascinated" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the plural subject "musings." Choice C is incorrect because the singular verb "fascinates" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the plural subject "musings." Choice D is incorrect because the singular verb "is fascinating" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the plural subject "musings."</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f10b7ce4","external_id":"5b4f4