rname":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061177,"updateDate":1755117061177}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061177, 1755117061177),
    ($SATQ$f1c5157d$SATQ$, $SATQ$ba593ea9-220c-4820-9652-e73ba28a2582$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Established in 1936 by African American novelist Richard Wright, <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> it would become a vital part of the creative movement known as the Chicago Black Renaissance. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"889108c4-7aa4-4249-ac11-9f41501fe1ef","content":"<p>the South Side Writers Group provided a valuable forum for Chicago writers to share ideas;</p>"},{"id":"cc85269b-cf58-4f11-95b8-dfb4b4d9363a","content":"<p>Chicago writers in the South Side Writers Group had a valuable forum for sharing ideas;&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"a8a3fcbe-0cbd-4f7f-a434-d7652f3b0fde","content":"<p>writers shared ideas at a valuable forum known as the South Side Writers Group in Chicago;</p>"},{"id":"90607736-9eae-42c7-bdf4-52ab00ed2bbd","content":"<p>Chicago was where the South Side Writers Group provided a valuable forum for writers to share ideas;&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["889108c4-7aa4-4249-ac11-9f41501fe1ef"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is subject-modifier placement. This choice makes the noun phrase &ldquo;the South Side Writers Group&rdquo; the subject of the sentence and places it immediately after the modifying phrase &ldquo;established in 1936 by African American novelist Richard Wright.&rdquo; In doing so, this choice clearly indicates that the South Side Writers Group&mdash;and not another noun in the sentence&mdash;was established in 1936 by Richard Wright.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because it results in a dangling modifier. The placement of the noun phrase &ldquo;Chicago writers&rdquo; immediately after the modifying phrase illogically suggests that the Chicago writers were established in 1936 by Richard Wright. Choice C is incorrect because it results in a dangling modifier. The placement of the noun phrase &ldquo;writers&rdquo; immediately after the modifying phrase illogically suggests that the writers were established in 1936 by Richard Wright. Choice D is incorrect because it results in a dangling modifier. The placement of the noun phrase &ldquo;Chicago&rdquo; immediately after the modifying phrase illogically suggests that Chicago was established in 1936 by Richard Wright.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f1c5157d","external_id":"ba593ea9-220c-4820-9652-e73ba28a2582","vaultid":null,"uId":"c549363b-5c28-4000-b69b-faee8a86ff8f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"FSS","skill_desc":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Established in 1936 by African American novelist Richard Wright, <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> it would become a vital part of the creative movement known as the Chicago Black Renaissance. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"889108c4-7aa4-4249-ac11-9f41501fe1ef","content":"<p>the South Side Writers Group provided a valuable forum for Chicago writers to share ideas;</p>"},{"id":"cc85269b-cf58-4f11-95b8-dfb4b4d9363a","content":"<p>Chicago writers in the South Side Writers Group had a valuable forum for sharing ideas;&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"a8a3fcbe-0cbd-4f7f-a434-d7652f3b0fde","content":"<p>writers shared ideas at a valuable forum known as the South Side Writers Group in Chicago;</p>"},{"id":"90607736-9eae-42c7-bdf4-52ab00ed2bbd","content":"<p>Chicago was where the South Side Writers Group provided a valuable forum for writers to share ideas;&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["889108c4-7aa4-4249-ac11-9f41501fe1ef"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is subject-modifier placement. This choice makes the noun phrase &ldquo;the South Side Writers Group&rdquo; the subject of the sentence and places it immediately after the modifying phrase &ldquo;established in 1936 by African American novelist Richard Wright.&rdquo; In doing so, this choice clearly indicates that the South Side Writers Group&mdash;and not another noun in the sentence&mdash;was established in 1936 by Richard Wright.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because it results in a dangling modifier. The placement of the noun phrase &ldquo;Chicago writers&rdquo; immediately after the modifying phrase illogically suggests that the Chicago writers were established in 1936 by Richard Wright. Choice C is incorrect because it results in a dangling modifier. The placement of the noun phrase &ldquo;writers&rdquo; immediately after the modifying phrase illogically suggests that the writers were established in 1936 by Richard Wright. Choice D is incorrect because it results in a dangling modifier. The placement of the noun phrase &ldquo;Chicago&rdquo; immediately after the modifying phrase illogically suggests that Chicago was established in 1936 by Richard Wright.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771170,"updateDate":1776362771170}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771170, 1776362771170),
    ($SATQ$f2eaaf5d$SATQ$, $SATQ$38e3e89e-703c-43e0-af99-00654ddf5fd8$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ab3ad652-7327-4acb-a895-fc219f44d0fa$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$BOU$SATQ$, $SATQ$Boundaries$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>At eight paragraphs long, the preamble to the constitution of <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> country in Western Asia&mdash;is much longer than the one-paragraph preamble to the United States Constitution.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"00fcf568-f12b-4ccc-b5d0-91b607ba1e48","content":"<p>Bahrain&mdash;a&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"98908f75-9436-4505-8c98-d6b18549af1e","content":"<p>Bahrain, a</p>"},{"id":"cfd42568-2fa1-40a3-b221-4da7ce524c13","content":"<p>Bahrain a</p>"},{"id":"71b5a3ab-d41f-4889-aeaf-932496f34b49","content":"<p>Bahrain: a</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["00fcf568-f12b-4ccc-b5d0-91b607ba1e48"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is the punctuation of a supplementary element within a sentence. The dash after &ldquo;Bahrain&rdquo; pairs with the dash after &ldquo;Asia&rdquo; to separate the supplementary element &ldquo;a country in Western Asia&rdquo; from the rest of the sentence.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because a comma can&rsquo;t be paired with a dash in this way to separate the supplementary element from the rest of the sentence. Choice C is incorrect because it fails to use appropriate punctuation to separate the supplementary element from the rest of the sentence. Choice D is incorrect because a colon can&rsquo;t be paired with a dash in this way to separate the supplementary element from the rest of the sentence. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-783-SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$4a1dc9ca-4da9-47a4-a0bd-bff33c537bf4$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f2eaaf5d","external_id":"38e3e89e-703c-43e0-af99-00654ddf5fd8","vaultid":"ab3ad652-7327-4acb-a895-fc219f44d0fa","uId":"e1815310-100b-4d80-9b38-79f9f4d970a4","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"BOU","skill_desc":"Boundaries","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>At eight paragraphs long, the preamble to the constitution of <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> country in Western Asia&mdash;is much longer than the one-paragraph preamble to the United States Constitution.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"00fcf568-f12b-4ccc-b5d0-91b607ba1e48","content":"<p>Bahrain&mdash;a&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"98908f75-9436-4505-8c98-d6b18549af1e","content":"<p>Bahrain, a</p>"},{"id":"cfd42568-2fa1-40a3-b221-4da7ce524c13","content":"<p>Bahrain a</p>"},{"id":"71b5a3ab-d41f-4889-aeaf-932496f34b49","content":"<p>Bahrain: a</p>"}],"keys":["00fcf568-f12b-4ccc-b5d0-91b607ba1e48"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is the punctuation of a supplementary element within a sentence. The dash after &ldquo;Bahrain&rdquo; pairs with the dash after &ldquo;Asia&rdquo; to separate the supplementary element &ldquo;a country in Western Asia&rdquo; from the rest of the sentence.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because a comma can&rsquo;t be paired with a dash in this way to separate the supplementary element from the rest of the sentence. Choice C is incorrect because it fails to use appropriate punctuation to separate the supplementary element from the rest of the sentence. Choice D is incorrect because a colon can&rsquo;t be paired with a dash in this way to separate the supplementary element from the rest of the sentence. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-783-SEC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"4a1dc9ca-4da9-47a4-a0bd-bff33c537bf4","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959353,"updateDate":1691007959353}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959353, 1691007959353),
    ($SATQ$f30a478e$SATQ$, $SATQ$cf47f4f6-bab4-44f6-82fd-17fbbf30c460$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$278686bb-da86-4d96-b5cd-d97a66564e44$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$BOU$SATQ$, $SATQ$Boundaries$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>A study published by Rice University geoscientist Ming Tang in 2019 offers a new explanation for the origin of Earth&rsquo;s <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> structures called arcs, towering ridges that form when a dense oceanic plate subducts under a less dense continental plate, melts in the mantle below, and then rises and bursts through the continental crust above.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"7ea42efa-78bc-42a1-866b-bbb3f8acafad","content":"<p>continents geological</p>"},{"id":"58866cd0-8463-4be8-b8ab-1f8f19b2f853","content":"<p>continents: geological</p>"},{"id":"7f40b5a6-eaee-4cba-b67b-a767d07128a9","content":"<p>continents; geological</p>"},{"id":"63ef0f17-9ce9-46c2-b676-a40ccbc90f64","content":"<p>continents. Geological</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["58866cd0-8463-4be8-b8ab-1f8f19b2f853"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The convention being tested is punctuation use between a main clause and a supplementary phrase. In this choice, a colon is correctly used to mark the boundary between the main clause (&ldquo;A study&hellip;continents&rdquo;) and the supplementary phrase (&ldquo;geological&hellip;above&rdquo;) and to introduce the following explanation of the origin of Earth&rsquo;s continents. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it fails to mark the boundary between the main clause (&ldquo;A study&hellip;continents&rdquo;) and the supplementary phrase (&ldquo;geological&hellip;above&rdquo;) with appropriate punctuation. Choice C is incorrect because a semicolon can&rsquo;t be used in this way to join the main clause (&ldquo;A study&hellip;continents&rdquo;) and the supplementary phrase (&ldquo;geological&hellip;above&rdquo;). A semicolon is conventionally used to join two main clauses, whereas a colon is conventionally used to introduce an element that explains or amplifies the information in the preceding clause, making it the better choice in this context. Choice D is incorrect because it results in a rhetorically unacceptable sentence fragment beginning with &ldquo;geological.&rdquo; </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-639-SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$67b410ea-e9cf-43cf-83f7-32818788292f$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f30a478e","external_id":"cf47f4f6-bab4-44f6-82fd-17fbbf30c460","vaultid":"278686bb-da86-4d96-b5cd-d97a66564e44","uId":"723f57db-dad4-4f97-bae0-2f21631763af","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"SEC","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill_cd":"BOU","skill_desc":"Boundaries","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>A study published by Rice University geoscientist Ming Tang in 2019 offers a new explanation for the origin of Earth&rsquo;s <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> structures called arcs, towering ridges that form when a dense oceanic plate subducts under a less dense continental plate, melts in the mantle below, and then rises and bursts through the continental crust above.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"7ea42efa-78bc-42a1-866b-bbb3f8acafad","content":"<p>continents geological</p>"},{"id":"58866cd0-8463-4be8-b8ab-1f8f19b2f853","content":"<p>continents: geological</p>"},{"id":"7f40b5a6-eaee-4cba-b67b-a767d07128a9","content":"<p>continents; geological</p>"},{"i